From 80aa753d7cad336be8cd4db16944554ba91ae9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:11:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: amlogic: add native SC2 HEVC and AV1 Request decoding

Add controls-authoritative HEVC/AV1 normalization, serialized hardware
contexts, factory secure-index loading, owned DMA references, bounded
completion and cancellation. Retire queued CAPTURE references in worker
order so an early QBUF does not invalidate an in-flight retained frame.

Main8 Request outputs, hidden AV1 references, mixed contexts and six
independent open/seek streams match independent software pixels on SC2.
Main10 exported scatter surfaces retain full ten-bit samples and survive
decoder teardown. Separate nominal compression-register header length
from the actual 64x64 scatter-map allocation, including output guards.

AMF0 is a local proposed ABI, not an upstream-assigned format. Tested
fixtures do not establish grain, frame-ID or super-resolution support;
this commit does not claim full Kodi or HDR/link acceptance.

Change-Id: I0147a02ffa57e41c8ecaf735e4761f26f30e9e43
